<section class="license-group" aria-labelledby="icons-heading">
  <h2 id="icons-heading">Interface icons (inlined as SVG markup at build time, no JavaScript)</h2>
  <p>
    Lucide icons are rendered into the HTML as inline SVG during the build. No icon font, no sprite
    sheet, and no JavaScript is shipped for them. Six icons are used in total:
    <code>chevron-down</code> appears in the site navigation on every page that renders it (30 of the
    34 built pages), and <code>arrow-left-right</code>, <code>arrow-right</code>,
    <code>chart-no-axes-column-increasing</code>, <code>file-search</code>, and
    <code>trash-2</code> appear only on the two home pages (<code>/</code> and <code>/ja/</code>).
    This page (<code>/licenses</code>) and the 404 pages contain no Lucide icons at all, because they
    do not render the site navigation.
  </p>
  <p>
    Lucide's own license file covers two different sets of icons, and both sets are present here.
    Icons that Lucide derives from the Feather project carry Feather's MIT license, and the rest
    carry Lucide's ISC license. Of the six icons above, <code>chevron-down</code>,
    <code>arrow-right</code>, and <code>trash-2</code> are Feather-derived (MIT); the other three are
    Lucide originals (ISC). Both notices are reproduced in the single license file linked below,
    exactly as Lucide distributes them.
  </p>

